# Line endings are part of this repository's contract, not a preference.
#
# Two gates compare bytes, not semantics:
#
#   verify:signature   regenerates src/constants/signature.ts and compares it to
#                      the committed file with strict string equality
#   verify:provenance  hashes committed assets, including the .txt licences, and
#                      requires an exact SHA-256 and byte count
#
# Both therefore depend on the working tree holding the same bytes that were
# reviewed. A clone on a machine configured with core.autocrlf=true would receive
# CRLF for every text file and fail both checks while the repository content was
# entirely unchanged, turning a reproducibility guarantee into a platform-specific
# one and producing a false failure in a security-adjacent gate.
#
# Pinning LF in the working tree makes "reproducible from a clean clone" true on
# every platform rather than only on the ones that happen not to rewrite bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched by end-of-line conversion. The fonts and the
# headshot are hash-locked in scripts/asset-provenance.json, so a single rewritten
# byte would break the provenance lock. Marked explicitly rather than relying on
# Git's content heuristic, because the heuristic is not part of any contract.
*.ttf   -text
*.woff2 -text
*.JPG   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.png   -text
*.ico   -text
